  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}z}\u00f7\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{6{z}^{3}}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}z}\u00f7\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{6{z}^{3}},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}z}\u00f7\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{6{z}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}z}\\cdot \\frac{6{z}^{3}}{7{x}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}\\cdot 2z}\\cdot \\frac{3\\cdot 2z\\cdot {z}^{2}}{7\\cdot {x}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{{y}^{2}\\cdot \\cancel{2z}}\\cdot \\frac{3\\cdot \\cancel{2z}\\cdot {z}^{2}}{7\\cdot \\cancel{{x}^{2}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3{z}^{2}}{7{y}^{2}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
